rs.\",28\r\n3207,ANTIOXIDANTES,\"Antioxidantes are compounds that play a significant role in health and wellness, particularly in the context of chronic kidney disease, where they may improve patient outcomes through dietary interventions. These substances are known for their ability to protect cells from damage caused by free radicals, which are unstable molecules that can lead to oxidative stress. This protective function is associated with various health benefits, including support for muscle health and cognitive function. Additionally, antioxidants are utilized in food preservation to prevent oxidation, with examples including citric acid and butylated hydroxyanisole. Overall, antioxidants are vital for maintaining cellular integrity and promoting overall health.\",3\r\n3165,MCI,\"Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI) is a condition that often precedes Alzheimer's disease. It is characterized by noticeable memory and cognitive difficulties, which are significant enough to be recognized but not severe enough to interfere significantly with daily life.\",4\r\n3215,FLAVONOIDES,\"Flavonoids are compounds known for their role as inhibitors or inducers of hepatic enzyme systems, which can modify drug bioavailability. Additionally, they are recognized as antioxidant compounds that may have beneficial effects on cardiovascular health.\",4\r\n3208,HOMOCISTEÍNA,\"Homocisteína is an amino acid that is produced during the metabolism of methionine and is formed from protein metabolism. It is known to accumulate in the body due to various metabolic disorders, which can lead to significant health issues. Elevated levels of homocisteína are associated with several problems, including cardiovascular diseases and cognitive decline, such as dementia. Additionally, high levels of this amino acid can damage blood vessels, further increasing the risk of cardiovascular complications. A deficiency in Vitamin B₁₂ can also lead to increased homocisteína levels, highlighting the importance of p